1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,730
Meena runs the bus stand Chai Corner,
and every morning Ravi hands her

2
00:00:04,730 --> 00:00:05,725
a new order.

3
00:00:06,025 --> 00:00:07,432
Monday, sell more.

4
00:00:07,432 --> 00:00:08,888
Tuesday, save milk.

5
00:00:08,888 --> 00:00:10,590
Wednesday, open earlier.

6
00:00:11,140 --> 00:00:13,953
Meena never gets a say,
so she stops trying.

7
00:00:14,253 --> 00:00:17,373
And at the end of the month,
nobody knows if she did well.

8
00:00:18,023 --> 00:00:19,563
Orders are not enough.

9
00:00:19,563 --> 00:00:22,304
Ravi and Meena need to set goals together.

10
00:00:23,004 --> 00:00:24,969
This idea has a name.

11
00:00:24,969 --> 00:00:27,792
Management by objectives, or MBO.

12
00:00:28,142 --> 00:00:31,982
It comes from Peter Drucker, the
Austrian born American thinker.

13
00:00:32,332 --> 00:00:37,407
In 1954, he described it in his
book, The Practice of Management.

14
00:00:37,757 --> 00:00:42,341
Manager and worker agree on clear
goals together, then judge the work by

15
00:00:42,341 --> 00:00:43,322
its results.

16
00:00:43,972 --> 00:00:45,926
So Ravi stops giving orders.

17
00:00:45,926 --> 00:00:47,890
He sits down with his team.

18
00:00:48,240 --> 00:00:51,562
Together, they agree one clear
goal for the bus stand outlet.

19
00:00:51,912 --> 00:00:54,410
Five hundred cups a day, by March.

20
00:00:54,410 --> 00:00:56,443
Ravi and Meena both say yes.

21
00:00:57,093 --> 00:00:59,956
Now watch MBO run, in five steps.

22
00:01:00,306 --> 00:01:01,206
One.

23
00:01:00,796 --> 00:01:03,169
Set the goal for the whole business.

24
00:01:03,169 --> 00:01:05,696
Five hundred cups a day at outlet two.

25
00:01:06,046 --> 00:01:06,946
Two.

26
00:01:06,534 --> 00:01:08,684
Set each person's goal, together.

27
00:01:08,684 --> 00:01:12,269
Meena suggests two hundred
cups before ten in the morning.

28
00:01:12,619 --> 00:01:13,519
Three.

29
00:01:13,226 --> 00:01:14,709
Make an action plan.

30
00:01:14,709 --> 00:01:18,649
An extra helper at seven, and
cups washed the night before.

31
00:01:18,999 --> 00:01:19,899
Four.

32
00:01:19,546 --> 00:01:20,689
Review progress.

33
00:01:20,689 --> 00:01:23,190
Every Friday, they check the numbers.

34
00:01:23,190 --> 00:01:26,511
In week five, sales dip,
and they fix it early.

35
00:01:26,861 --> 00:01:27,761
Five.

36
00:01:27,425 --> 00:01:28,865
Appraise and reward.

37
00:01:28,865 --> 00:01:33,477
By March, Meena hits two hundred,
and earns a bonus for the result.

38
00:01:34,127 --> 00:01:35,769
Why does MBO work?

39
00:01:36,119 --> 00:01:37,019
Clarity.

40
00:01:36,884 --> 00:01:39,200
Meena knows exactly what counts.

41
00:01:39,550 --> 00:01:40,450
Motivation.

42
00:01:40,322 --> 00:01:43,194
She chose the target,
so she wants to hit it.

43
00:01:43,544 --> 00:01:44,703
Participation.

44
00:01:44,703 --> 00:01:46,954
The worker gets a real say.

45
00:01:47,304 --> 00:01:48,677
And fair appraisal.

46
00:01:48,677 --> 00:01:51,752
She is judged on results,
not on Ravi's mood.

47
00:01:52,402 --> 00:01:55,099
So what does MBO look like at work today?

48
00:01:55,449 --> 00:01:56,654
Cascading goals.

49
00:01:56,654 --> 00:02:00,579
A company's yearly goal is
split into goals for every team.

50
00:02:00,929 --> 00:02:02,706
Objectives and key results.

51
00:02:02,706 --> 00:02:06,985
Many companies set a few big goals
each quarter, with numbers to track

52
00:02:06,985 --> 00:02:07,885
them.

53
00:02:07,876 --> 00:02:09,057
Agreed targets.

54
00:02:09,057 --> 00:02:13,651
A sales manager and each salesperson
agree the year's target together.

55
00:02:14,001 --> 00:02:14,901
Reviews.

56
00:02:14,725 --> 00:02:19,588
Every quarter, a manager and an employee
check progress against the goals.

57
00:02:19,938 --> 00:02:20,838
Rewards.

58
00:02:20,701 --> 00:02:24,688
A bonus is paid for results
that were agreed in advance.

59
00:02:25,338 --> 00:02:27,507
But does MBO always work?

60
00:02:27,507 --> 00:02:28,616
Not always.

61
00:02:28,966 --> 00:02:30,011
The good side.

62
00:02:30,011 --> 00:02:32,803
Clear goals, more
effort, and fair reviews.

63
00:02:33,153 --> 00:02:34,262
The hard side.

64
00:02:34,262 --> 00:02:37,907
It takes many meetings, and
goals can be set too easy.

65
00:02:38,257 --> 00:02:42,140
And if Ravi only counts cups,
the taste of the chai may slip.

66
00:02:42,490 --> 00:02:48,085
A 1991 review of seventy studies
found productivity rose in sixty eight

67
00:02:48,085 --> 00:02:49,082
of them.

68
00:02:49,432 --> 00:02:52,957
The gains were biggest when
top managers truly backed it.

69
00:02:53,307 --> 00:02:54,862
So the lesson is simple.

70
00:02:54,862 --> 00:02:58,380
Agree the goal together, and
keep the real purpose in view.

71
00:02:59,030 --> 00:03:00,001
Quick check.

72
00:03:00,001 --> 00:03:03,902
Ravi writes Meena's targets
alone, and just hands them over.

73
00:03:03,902 --> 00:03:05,963
Which part of MBO is missing?

74
00:03:07,863 --> 00:03:08,947
Participation!

75
00:03:08,947 --> 00:03:12,863
In MBO, the manager and the
worker set goals together.

76
00:03:13,463 --> 00:03:14,472
So, remember.

77
00:03:14,772 --> 00:03:19,619
MBO means agreeing clear goals together,
and judging the work by results.

78
00:03:19,969 --> 00:03:24,816
It runs in five steps: business goals,
personal goals, action plans, review,

79
00:03:24,816 --> 00:03:25,716
and reward.

80
00:03:26,045 --> 00:03:30,288
It brings clarity and motivation,
but keep the real purpose in view.

81
00:03:30,888 --> 00:03:35,991
Next time, Ravi faces a big choice,
and learns the decision making process.
